  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduce Early Marriages to Enhance Gender Equality</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at achieving an enabling legal, social environment to curtail early marriages, and enhaced awareness of women and girls to dignified reproductive health rights services in Punjab province. The outcomes of the project are (1) Improved Punjab Marriage Restraint (Amendment) Act 2015 ensures minimum age for girls set at 18 years, and (2) Increased knowledge of sexual and reproductive health rights and available health services for women and adolescents girls in Punjab. The target group of the project are girls and boys under 18 years of age, teachers, health workers and legislators. The project will also target inclusion of persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
